<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" dir="ltr">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, viewport-fit=cover">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#2a3f5f">
<title>Parasitology — 50 Q &amp; A (Per-Question Grading)</title>
<style>
:root{
  --bg:#f6f4ef; --bg2:#ebe6db; --card:#ffffff; --ink:#1a2138; --muted:#6b6a63;
  --line:#d9d3c4; --accent:#2a3f5f; --accent-soft:#dfe5ef; --accent2:#b87333;
  --accent2-soft:#f4e7d5; --gold:#b8873a; --gold-soft:#faf0dc;
  --danger:#b3261e; --danger-soft:#fbe8e6; --ok:#2e7d5b; --ok-soft:#e2f3ea;
  --rose:#5c6b8a; --rose-soft:#e6ebf3; --mauve:#8a7d99; --mauve-soft:#efecf3;
  --radius:18px; --shadow:0 6px 20px rgba(45,55,80,.10);
}
[data-theme="dark"]{
  --bg:#080b12; --bg2:#101521; --card:#171e2c; --ink:#e6eef5; --muted:#a8b0bc;
  --line:#28313f; --accent:#a8bcda; --accent-soft:#181f30; --accent2:#d9a87a;
  --accent2-soft:#2a1e14; --gold:#e0b062; --gold-soft:#2a2113;
  --danger:#ff8a80; --danger-soft:#2e1a18; --ok:#7ee2a8; --ok-soft:#12291c;
  --rose:#b0c0dc; --rose-soft:#181f30; --mauve:#c0b4cc; --mauve-soft:#171e2c;
  --shadow:0 6px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.55);
}
*{box-sizing:border-box;-webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent}
html{scroll-behavior:smooth}
body{
  margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font-size:16px;line-height:1.85;
  font-family:"Segoe UI","Noto Naskh Arabic","Tahoma",system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif;
  transition:background .3s,color .3s;overflow-x:hidden;padding-bottom:20px;
}
.wrap{max-width:840px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 14px 130px}

header.top{
  position:sticky;top:0;z-index:60;background:var(--bg);
  border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);box-shadow:0 2px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.04);
}
.top-in{max-width:840px;margin:0 auto;padding:10px 14px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px}
.logo{
  width:40px;height:40px;border-radius:12px;flex:none;
  background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--accent),var(--accent2));
  display:grid;place-items:center;color:#fff;font-weight:800;font-size:17px;
}
.titles{flex:1;min-width:0}
.titles h1{margin:0;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.2px;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
.titles p{margin:0;font-size:10.5px;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
.hbtns{display:flex;gap:6px;flex:none}
.icon-btn{
  border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--card);color:var(--ink);
  width:40px;height:40px;border-radius:12px;font-size:16px;cursor:pointer;flex:none;
  display:grid;place-items:center;transition:.2s;
}
.icon-btn:active{transform:scale(.92)}
.icon-btn.on{background:var(--accent);color:#fff;border-color:var(--accent)}

.card{
  background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius);
  padding:16px;margin:14px 0;box-shadow:var(--shadow);
  overflow-wrap:break-word;word-wrap:break-word;
}
.card h2{
  margin:0 0 12px;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:var(--accent);
  display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;line-height:1.45;flex-wrap:wrap;
}
.card h2 .num{
  background:var(--accent-soft);color:var(--accent);width:32px;height:32px;flex:none;
  border-radius:10px;display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;
}
.muted{color:var(--muted);font-size:14px}

.box{border-radius:14px;padding:13px 15px;margin:12px 0;border:1px solid;font-size:15px;line-height:1.85}
.box .bt{font-weight:800;display:block;margin-bottom:6px;font-size:14.5px}
.box.def{background:var(--accent-soft);border-color:var(--accent)}
.box.def .bt{color:var(--accent)}
.box.tip{background:var(--gold-soft);border-color:var(--gold)}
.box.tip .bt{color:var(--gold)}
.box.warn{background:var(--danger-soft);border-color:var(--danger)}
.box.warn .bt{color:var(--danger)}

.btn{
  border:none;border-radius:14px;padding:12px 18px;font-family:inherit;font-size:15px;
  font-weight:800;cursor:pointer;transition:.15s;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;
  justify-content:center;gap:7px;line-height:1.4;
}
.btn:active{transform:scale(.97)}
.btn.p{background:var(--accent);color:#fff}
.btn.g{background:var(--gold);color:#fff}
.btn.o{background:var(--card);color:var(--ink);border:1.5px solid var(--line)}

/* Question Card Styles */
.qcard{
  background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:16px;
  padding:15px;margin:14px 0;box-shadow:var(--shadow);scroll-margin-top:80px;
  overflow-wrap:break-word;word-wrap:break-word;
}
.qhead{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;margin-bottom:11px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.qnum{
  background:var(--accent);color:#fff;width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:10px;
  display:grid;place-items:center;font-weight:800;font-size:14px;flex:none;
}
.chip{
  font-size:11px;font-weight:800;background:var(--bg2);color:var(--muted);
  border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:20px;padding:3px 11px;line-height:1.4;
}
.qtext{font-size:15.5px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.8;margin:0 0 12px;overflow-wrap:break-word}
.opts{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px}
.opt{
  border:1.5px solid var(--line);background:var(--bg);border-radius:12px;
  padding:11px 13px;font-size:14.5px;cursor:pointer;transition:.15s;display:flex;
  gap:10px;align-items:flex-start;line-height:1.7;overflow-wrap:break-word;
}
.opt .mk{
  width:20px;height:20px;border-radius:50%;border:2px solid var(--muted);flex:none;
  margin-top:4px;display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:11px;font-weight:800;color:#fff;
  transition:.15s;
}
.opt .otxt{flex:1;min-width:0}
.opt.sel{border-color:var(--accent);background:var(--accent-soft)}
.opt.sel .mk{border-color:var(--accent);background:var(--accent)}
.opt.right{border-color:var(--ok);background:var(--ok-soft)}
.opt.right .mk{border-color:var(--ok);background:var(--ok)}
.opt.wrong{border-color:var(--danger);background:var(--danger-soft)}
.opt.wrong .mk{border-color:var(--danger);background:var(--danger)}
.opt.lock{cursor:default}

.qacts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:7px;margin-top:12px}
.qacts .btn{padding:9px 6px;font-size:12.5px;border-radius:11px;width:100%}

.fb{
  margin-top:12px;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;font-size:14.5px;
  display:none;line-height:1.9;overflow-wrap:break-word;
}
.fb.show{display:block;animation:fade .25s}
@keyframes fade{from{opacity:0;transform:translateY(-4px)}to{opacity:1;transform:none}}
.fb.ok{background:var(--ok-soft);border:1px solid var(--ok)}
.fb.no{background:var(--danger-soft);border:1px solid var(--danger)}
.fb.hint{background:var(--gold-soft);border:1px solid var(--gold)}
.fb .ttl{font-weight:800;display:block;margin-bottom:8px;font-size:15px}
.fb .why{display:block;margin:6px 0}
.fb .why b{color:var(--accent)}
.fb .trap{
  display:block;background:var(--gold-soft);border-left:4px solid var(--gold);
  padding:8px 12px;border-radius:6px;margin-top:10px;font-size:13.5px;
}
.fb.no .trap{background:var(--danger-soft);border-left-color:var(--danger)}
.fb .trap b{color:var(--gold)}
.fb.no .trap b{color:var(--danger)}

.parttitle{
  margin:30px 0 8px;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:var(--rose);
  display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;line-height:1.5;
}
.parttitle::before{content:"";width:5px;height:22px;background:var(--rose);border-radius:4px;flex:none}

.bar{height:11px;background:var(--bg2);border-radius:20px;overflow:hidden;margin:6px 0 2px}
.bar > i{display:block;height:100%;background:var(--accent);border-radius:20px;transition:width .6s}

.footnote{text-align:center;color:var(--muted);font-size:12.5px;padding:28px 0 8px;line-height:1.9}
::-webkit-scrollbar{height:8px;width:8px}
::-webkit-scrollbar-track{background:var(--bg2)}
::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb{background:var(--line);border-radius:4px}

@media (max-width:420px){
  body{font-size:15.5px}
  .card{padding:14px 13px}
  .card h2{font-size:17px}
  .titles h1{font-size:12.5px}
  .titles p{font-size:10px}
  .qtext{font-size:15px}
  .btn{font-size:14px;padding:11px 14px}
  .qacts{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header class="top">
  <div class="top-in">
    <div class="logo">🪱</div>
    <div class="titles">
      <h1>Parasitology — 50 Q &amp; A</h1>
      <p>Per-question grading · Hint per question · Deep explanations</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hbtns">
      <button class="icon-btn" id="themeBtn" title="Toggle dark mode">🌙</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="wrap">

  <div class="card">
    <h2><span class="num">✦</span> 50 Questions — Per-Question Grading</h2>
    <p class="muted">Answer each question, then tap <b>✓ Check</b> to grade it individually. A 💡 <b>Hint</b> is available for every question — it never gives the answer. Progress is saved.</p>
    <div style="margin-top:14px">
      <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)">
        <span>Progress</span><span id="progTxt">0 / 50</span>
      </div>
      <div class="bar"><i id="progBar" style="width:0%"></i></div>
    </div>
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:10px;margin-top:14px">
      <button class="btn g" id="gradeAllBtn">✓ Grade All</button>
      <button class="btn o" id="resetAllBtn">↺ Reset</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id="quiz"></div>

  <div class="footnote">
    50 Questions — 30 MCQs + 20 True/False<br>
    Per-question grading · Hints without revealing answers · Progress saved locally ✦
  </div>
</div>

<script>
/* ============================================================
   0) STORAGE
   ============================================================ */
const STORE = {
  get(k, def){
    try{ const v = localStorage.getItem('pq50-' + k); return v === null ? def : JSON.parse(v); }
    catch(e){ return def; }
  },
  set(k, v){ try{ localStorage.setItem('pq50-' + k, JSON.stringify(v)); }catch(e){} },
  del(k){ try{ localStorage.removeItem('pq50-' + k); }catch(e){} }
};

/* ============================================================
   1) DARK MODE
   ============================================================ */
const themeBtn = document.getElementById('themeBtn');
function setTheme(t){
  document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', t);
  themeBtn.textContent = t === 'dark' ? '☀️' : '🌙';
  STORE.set('theme', t);
}
setTheme(STORE.get('theme', 'light'));
themeBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
  setTheme(document.documentElement.getAttribute('data-theme') === 'dark' ? 'light' : 'dark');
});

/* ============================================================
   2) SPEECH (simple)
   ============================================================ */
document.addEventListener('click', e => {
  const btn = e.target.closest('[data-speak]');
  if(!btn) return;
  if(!('speechSynthesis' in window)) return;
  window.speechSynthesis.cancel();
  const u = new SpeechSynthesisUtterance(btn.dataset.speak);
  u.lang = 'en-US'; u.rate = 0.95;
  window.speechSynthesis.speak(u);
});

/* ============================================================
   3) QUESTION BANK — 30 MCQ + 20 TF
   Each question:
     type: 'mcq' | 'tf'
     part: level label
     topic: chip
     q: question text
     options: array (for MCQ) — TF uses ['True','False']
     ans: index of correct option
     hint: conceptual pointer (NOT the answer)
     explain: full HTML (why correct + why others wrong)
     trap: the specific trap
   ============================================================ */
const QUESTIONS = [
/* ===== PART 1: 30 MCQs ===== */
/* Level 1 — Foundation */
{n:1, part:'Level 1 · Foundation &amp; Definitions', type:'mcq', topic:'Biodiversity',
 q:'The term "Biodiversity" encompasses all of the following levels EXCEPT:',
 options:['Genetic diversity','Species diversity','Ecosystem diversity','Cellular diversity'],
 ans:3,
 hint:'Biodiversity is officially defined at three standard levels — genes, species, and ecosystems. Which of the four options is NOT one of those three?',
 explain:'<span class="why"><b>Why correct (D):</b> Biodiversity has three recognized levels: Genetic, Species, and Ecosystem. "Cellular diversity" is not a recognized level.</span><span class="why"><b>Why others are wrong:</b> (A), (B), (C) — all three are the exact levels taught in the lecture.</span>',
 trap:'"Species richness" or "cellular diversity" may appear as distractors — remember: only 3 levels are official.'},

{n:2, part:'Level 1 · Foundation &amp; Definitions', type:'mcq', topic:'Taxonomy',
 q:'Who is considered the "Father of Taxonomy" and introduced Binomial Nomenclature?',
 options:['Aristotle','John Ray','Carl Linnaeus','Charles Darwin'],
 ans:2,
 hint:'The "Father of Taxonomy" is the one who introduced the two-word naming system (Genus + species). Which option matches?',
 explain:'<span class="why"><b>Why correct (C):</b> Linnaeus created Binomial Nomenclature (Genus + species) and the 7 ranks.</span><span class="why"><b>Why others are wrong:</b> (A) Aristotle classified by blood/movement. (B) John Ray introduced the species concept but not the naming system. (D) Darwin = evolution.</span>',
 trap:'Do not confuse "Father of Taxonomy" (Linnaeus) with "Father of Evolution" (Darwin) or "Father of Classification" (Aristotle).'},

{n:3, part:'Level 1 · Foundation &amp; Definitions', type:'mcq', topic:'Binomial Nomenclature',
 q:'In the scientific name Homo sapiens, which statement is entirely CORRECT?',
 options:['Homo is the species, sapiens is the genus','Homo is the genus (capitalized), sapiens is the specific epithet (lowercase)','Both words must be capitalized','The name must always be written in English'],
 ans:1,
 hint:'Binomial rules: the first word has a bigger capital letter than the second. Which option matches this pattern?',
 explain:'<span class="why"><b>Why correct (B):</b> First word = Genus (capitalized). Second = species (lowercase). Both italicized.</span><span class="why"><b>Why others are wrong:</b> (A) Reversed. (C) Both capitalized is grammatically wrong. (D) Scientific names are Latin/Latinized, not English.</span>',
 trap:'Only the genus is capitalized. The specific epithet (species) is ALWAYS lowercase — even when written at the start of a sentence.'},

{n:4, part:'Level 1 · Foundation &amp; Definitions', type:'mcq', topic:'Joints',
 q:'A joint that is immovable and united by fibrous tissue is called:',
 options:['Synarthrosis','Amphiarthrosis','Diarthrosis','Symphysis'],
 ans:0,
 hint:'Break down the terms: "A-" means without, "-arthrosis" refers to joint. Which type of joint is immovable?',
 explain:'<span class="why"><b>Why correct (A):</b> Fibrous joints = Synarthrosis = immovable.</span><span class="why"><b>Why others are wrong:</b> (B) Amphiarthrosis = cartilaginous (slightly movable). (C) Diarthrosis = synovial (freely movable). (D) Symphysis = a type of slightly movable cartilaginous joint.</span>',
 trap:'"A" = without, so Synarthrosis = without movement. That is the immovable one.'},

/* Level 2 — Protozoa & Planaria */
{n:5, part:'Level 2 · Protozoa &amp; Planaria', type:'mcq', topic:'Amoeba',
 q:'Which of the following is the primary function of the contractile vacuole in Amoeba?',
 options:['Ingestion of food','Osmoregulation (expelling excess water)','Sexual reproduction','Locomotion'],
 ans:1,
 hint:'Amoeba lives in freshwater. Without a mechanism to remove water, what would happen to the cell?',
 explain:'<span class="why"><b>Why correct (B):</b> The contractile vacuole pumps out excess water to prevent the amoeba from bursting (osmoregulation).</span><span class="why"><b>Why others are wrong:</b> (A) Food uptake = phagocytosis/food vacuole. (C) Reproduction is not its role. (D) Locomotion = pseudopodia.</span>',
 trap:'Do not confuse "contractile" (contracts to expel water) with "food vacuole" (digestion).'},

{n:6, part:'Level 2 · Protozoa &amp; Planaria', type:'mcq', topic:'Entamoeba',
 q:'The infective stage of Entamoeba histolytica is:',
 options:['Trophozoite','Mature cyst with four nuclei','Immature cyst','Sporozoite'],
 ans:1,
 hint:'The infective stage must survive the acidic stomach. Which stage is the resistant one — active feeding or the cyst?',
 explain:'<span class="why"><b>Why correct (B):</b> The quadrinucleate cyst is the resistant stage swallowed via contaminated food/water.</span><span class="why"><b>Why others are wrong:</b> (A) Trophozoite is fragile and cannot survive stomach acid. (C) Immature cyst is not yet fully infective. (D) Sporozoite belongs to other protozoa (e.g., Plasmodium).</span>',
 trap:'Trophozoite = active feeding stage. Cyst = infective stage. Do not swap them.'},

{n:7, part:'Level 2 · Protozoa &amp; Planaria', type:'mcq', topic:'Planaria',
 q:'Planaria belongs to Class Turbellaria. How is its nervous system described?',
 options:['Diffuse nerve net','Ladder-like','Dorsal hollow nerve cord','Absent'],
 ans:1,
 hint:'Two longitudinal nerve cords connected by transverse nerves give a specific geometric image. Which option matches that image?',
 explain:'<span class="why"><b>Why correct (B):</b> Ladder-like — bilobed brain + 2 longitudinal nerve cords + transverse nerves.</span><span class="why"><b>Why others are wrong:</b> (A) Diffuse nerve net = Cnidaria. (C) Dorsal hollow nerve cord = Chordata. (D) Not absent.</span>',
 trap:'Cnidaria has a diffuse nerve net, Chordata has a hollow nerve cord, but Planaria has the ladder-like pattern.'},

{n:8, part:'Level 2 · Protozoa &amp; Planaria', type:'mcq', topic:'Planaria',
 q:'Which structure in Planaria detects light?',
 options:['Auricles','Ocelli','Flame cells','Pharynx'],
 ans:1,
 hint:'"Oculo-" is a Latin root related to eyes. Which term matches that root?',
 explain:'<span class="why"><b>Why correct (B):</b> Ocelli are the eyespots (photoreceptors).</span><span class="why"><b>Why others are wrong:</b> (A) Auricles = chemoreceptors. (C) Flame cells = excretion. (D) Pharynx = feeding.</span>',
 trap:'"Ocelli" looks like "ocelli" (eyes) — Auricles are ear-like (chemical detection).'},

{n:9, part:'Level 2 · Protozoa &amp; Planaria', type:'mcq', topic:'Planaria',
 q:'The digestive system of Planaria is incomplete because:',
 options:['It lacks a mouth','It lacks an anus','It has no intestine','It absorbs food through the skin'],
 ans:1,
 hint:'"Incomplete" in a digestive context means only one opening. Which opening is missing?',
 explain:'<span class="why"><b>Why correct (B):</b> It is a blind sac. The mouth serves for ingestion and egestion — no separate anus.</span><span class="why"><b>Why others are wrong:</b> (A) It has a mouth. (C) It has an intestine (3 branches). (D) Absorption through the skin is not the reason.</span>',
 trap:'"Incomplete" = missing anus. Do not mistake it for "missing mouth".'},

/* Level 3 — Trematodes */
{n:10, part:'Level 3 · Trematodes (Fasciola &amp; Schistosoma)', type:'mcq', topic:'Fasciola',
 q:'What is the infective stage of Fasciola for the definitive host (sheep)?',
 options:['Miracidium','Cercaria','Metacercaria','Redia'],
 ans:2,
 hint:'The infective stage must survive on grass until the sheep eats it. Which stage is encysted and resistant?',
 explain:'<span class="why"><b>Why correct (C):</b> Metacercaria — encysted on aquatic grass, eaten by sheep.</span><span class="why"><b>Why others are wrong:</b> (A) Miracidium infects the snail. (B) Cercaria leaves the snail and swims. (D) Redia is inside the snail.</span>',
 trap:'Miracidium → snail. Cercaria → free swimming. Metacercaria → eaten by sheep. Do not swap these.'},

{n:11, part:'Level 3 · Trematodes (Fasciola &amp; Schistosoma)', type:'mcq', topic:'Schistosoma',
 q:'Which parasite is an exception to the rule that Platyhelminthes are hermaphrodites?',
 options:['Fasciola hepatica','Taenia saginata','Schistosoma','Planaria'],
 ans:2,
 hint:'Most flatworms are hermaphrodites — one is dioecious. Which one has a male and a female?',
 explain:'<span class="why"><b>Why correct (C):</b> Schistosoma has separate sexes (dioecious) — male carries female in gynaecophoric canal.</span><span class="why"><b>Why others are wrong:</b> (A), (B), (D) — all hermaphrodites.</span>',
 trap:'Schistosoma is the ONLY hermaphrodite exception. Always remember it.'},

{n:12, part:'Level 3 · Trematodes (Fasciola &amp; Schistosoma)', type:'mcq', topic:'Schistosoma',
 q:'The egg of Schistosoma haematobium is characterized by a:',
 options:['Lateral spine','Terminal spine','Thick striated shell','Operculum'],
 ans:1,
 hint:'The name "haematobium" is associated with the urinary tract. Its egg has a spine at the END — which term means "end"?',
 explain:'<span class="why"><b>Why correct (B):</b> Haematobium = terminal spine (at the end).</span><span class="why"><b>Why others are wrong:</b> (A) Mansoni = lateral spine (on the side). (C) Taenia egg is thick radially striated. (D) Fasciola egg is operculated.</span>',
 trap:'Mansoni → Lateral. Haematobium → Terminal. Remember: HaemaTOBIUM has the "T" for Terminal.'},

{n:13, part:'Level 3 · Trematodes (Fasciola &amp; Schistosoma)', type:'mcq', topic:'Schistosoma',
 q:'The intermediate host for Schistosoma mansoni is the:',
 options:['Bulinus snail','Biomphalaria snail','Lymnaea snail','Cow'],
 ans:1,
 hint:'Two snails are famous — Bulinus and Biomphalaria. Which one matches "mansoni"?',
 explain:'<span class="why"><b>Why correct (B):</b> Biomphalaria = mansoni.</span><span class="why"><b>Why others are wrong:</b> (A) Bulinus = haematobium. (C) Lymnaea = Fasciola. (D) Cow = Taenia saginata.</span>',
 trap:'Biomphalaria → mansoni. Bulinus → haematobium. Match each snail to its species.'},

{n:14, part:'Level 3 · Trematodes (Fasciola &amp; Schistosoma)', type:'mcq', topic:'Fasciola',
 q:'A patient presents with "Halzoun" disease (parasitic pharyngitis). This is caused by:',
 options:['Schistosoma cercaria','Adult Fasciola worms attaching to the pharynx','Taenia cysts in the brain','Entamoeba in the liver'],
 ans:1,
 hint:'"Halzoun" is associated with eating a specific organ raw. Which parasite would end up in that organ in its adult form?',
 explain:'<span class="why"><b>Why correct (B):</b> Halzoun = human eats raw infected liver → adult Fasciola escape and attach to the pharynx.</span><span class="why"><b>Why others are wrong:</b> (A) Schistosoma cercaria penetrates skin. (C) Taenia cysts cause neurocysticercosis, not pharyngitis. (D) Entamoeba can cause liver abscess, not pharyngitis.</span>',
 trap:'Halzoun requires eating RAW LIVER. This is different from Fascioliasis caused by eating metacercariae on grass.'},

{n:15, part:'Level 3 · Trematodes (Fasciola &amp; Schistosoma)', type:'mcq', topic:'Fasciola',
 q:'The drug of choice for Fasciola (effective against both immature and adult flukes) is:',
 options:['Praziquantel','Triclabendazole','Metronidazole','Penicillin'],
 ans:1,
